{"absolutePath":"N03_SenderKeyedBalance.sol","exportedSymbols":{"N03_SenderKeyedBalance":[26]},"id":27,"license":"MIT","nodeType":"SourceUnit","nodes":[{"id":1,"literals":["solidity","^","0.8",".20"],"nodeType":"PragmaDirective","src":"32:24:0"},{"abstract":false,"baseContracts":[],"canonicalName":"N03_SenderKeyedBalance","contractDependencies":[],"contractKind":"contract","documentation":{"id":2,"nodeType":"StructuredDocumentation","src":"58:1985:0","text":"ISOLATES: a slot the unit writes that is keyed by the CALLER, in a unit\n that has NO address parameter at all.\n WHY THIS EXACT SHAPE. `propose_slot_vars` used to draw mapping keys only\n from the unit's PARAMETER list. `deposit(uint256)` has no address\n parameter, so for this contract the proposer produced NOT ONE candidate\n slot name -- the only slot the unit writes was never mentioned to the\n ladder, the ladder therefore returned no state rung, and the emitted PUT\n carried an empty oracle. That is the corpus shape too:\n `FarmingPool.deposit(uint256 amount)` writes `_balances[msg.sender]` and\n declares no address parameter either.\n Ten lines, one mapping, one level, one writer, no guards beyond `amt > 0`,\n no external calls, no library: if the chain\n     propose `bal[msg.sender]` -> ladder decides a rung -> emitter renders\n     the read at the PRANKED address -> forge green\n does not close here, nothing about the failure can be blamed on contract\n complexity, on nesting, or on the solver's mapping backend.\n EXPECTED, written before the run so the result cannot be reinterpreted:\n   1. the proposer offers `bal[msg.sender]` (before the change: nothing);\n   2. the ladder decides at least `post > pre` on it, and with --propose-r2\n      the delta rung `post - pre in [amt, amt] with post >= pre`;\n   3. the emitted .t.sol reads the slot at\n      `keccak256(abi.encode(<the expression the prank uses>, uint256(0)))`\n      -- NOT at the test contract's own address;\n   4. `forge test` is GREEN on the unmodified contract.\n NEGATIVE CONTROL, which is the half that can actually fail silently: if the\n region says nothing about `msg.sender`, the emitter must still REFUSE the\n key with its existing wording rather than hash whatever the test's own\n sender happens to be. A green test that established nothing looks exactly\n like a green test that established everything."},"fullyImplemented":true,"id":26,"linearizedBaseContracts":[26],"name":"N03_SenderKeyedBalance","nameLocation":"2052:22:0","nodeType":"ContractDefinition","nodes":[{"constant":false,"functionSelector":"5580f72a","id":6,"mutability":"mutable","name":"bal","nameLocation":"2116:3:0","nodeType":"VariableDeclaration","scope":26,"src":"2081:38:0","stateVariable":true,"storageLocation":"default","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_mapping$_t_address_$_t_uint256_$","typeString":"mapping(address => uint256)"},"typeName":{"id":5,"keyName":"","keyNameLocation":"-1:-1:-1","keyType":{"id":3,"name":"address","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"2089:7:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_address","typeString":"address"}},"nodeType":"Mapping","src":"2081:27:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_mapping$_t_address_$_t_uint256_$","typeString":"mapping(address => uint256)"},"valueName":"","valueNameLocation":"-1:-1:-1","valueType":{"id":4,"name":"uint256","nodeType":"ElementaryTypeName","src":"2100:7:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}}},"visibility":"public"},{"body":{"id":24,"nodeType":"Block","src":"2165:65:0","statements":[{"expression":{"arguments":[{"commonType":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"},"id":14,"isConstant":false,"isLValue":false,"isPure":false,"lValueRequested":false,"leftExpression":{"id":12,"name":"amt","nodeType":"Identifier","overloadedDeclarations":[],"referencedDeclaration":8,"src":"2183:3:0","typeDescriptions":{"typeIdentifier":"t_uint256","typeString":"uint256"}},"nodeType":"BinaryOperation","operator":">","rightExpres